## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Initial Story Editor run on script v01 (early morning)** — failed because: `SREV_MAX_TOKENS=3000` — Sonnet hit max_tokens before closing JSON block (output 11237-12246 chars). Fixed: bumped to 12000.
- **`requestRevision` re-triggering producing agent** — failed because: route only flipped asset status, no Inngest event dispatched. Pipeline stalled until manual `triggerAgent`. Fixed: `revisionEventForAsset(file_type)` map in approve route auto-fires.
- **Writer v02 — revisionNote was silently dropped** — failed because: 3 chained bugs. (1) factory.ts didn't forward `revisionNote` from event data. (2) runner.ts EXEC-SW case only passed `inputs`. (3) screenwriter.ts prompt said "Apply the **minimum change** needed, do not rewrite scenes that were not flagged" — opposite of restructure intent. Result: v02 had 80s/9 scenes/10s blocks, worse than v01. Fixed all 3 layers.
- **Story Editor gate (post-Writer v02)** — failed because: `Upstream gate failed for EXEC-SREV: Script (need 1, found 0 APPROVED)` — gate required APPROVED, but script v02 was REVIEW. Chicken-and-egg deadlock: Story Editor IS the gate FROM REVIEW to APPROVED. Fixed: `AgentDependency.allowedStatuses` field, SREV accepts REVIEW/REVISION/APPROVED.
- **Story Editor runner internal precondition (second layer)** — failed because: after gate fix, runner's `findApprovedAsset` still required `status === 'APPROVED'`. Fixed: accept REVIEW/REVISION/APPROVED in same function.
- **Approval gate misfires on long Director messages** — failed because: mid-sentence "нет" triggered rejection BEFORE later "одобряю" was scanned. Fixed: position-aware verdict (later token wins) via `approvalPosition()` + `rejectionPosition()` + `verdictForTurn()`.
- **`reasoning_effort=low` on gpt-5.5** — failed because: model spent all 2000 max_completion_tokens on invisible reasoning_tokens (2500 burned, 0 chars output, finish_reason=length). Fixed: `OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=none` (env already set yesterday, validated today still works).
- **Mock supabase `.in()` missing** — failed because: replay-pilot crashed `baseQuery.in is not a function`. Fixed: added `.in()` method to mock-supabase.
- **PA self-QA hallucinated tolerance** — failed because: Writer v02 self-QA wrote "80 seconds ≈60 target; within tolerance at 33% over". Fixed: screenwriter prompt now explicitly forbids this — "80s ≈ 60s within tolerance is a failure, not tolerance".
- **`enrichBible` already-enriched lock** — failed because: route returns "Asset already enriched — use /regenerate-image to reroll the image" but PA had no `regenerate-image` tool. Fixed: new `regenerateBibleImage` PA tool.

