## Decisions Made

- **Merge style `--merge`** — reason: preserves 227 auto-sync commits as audit trail of iterative Mode 2.5 / Mode 3 development; valuable evidence base for future Director directives. Squash would have lost this diary.
- **Skill correction over orchestration hardcoding** (Director directive 17:01) — when bugs appear, fix the agent's prompt first; touch routing only when prompt fix is insufficient. Codified in `technology.md §7.4`.
- **Internal loop closure before Director** (Director directive 16:59) — Writer↔Story Editor must converge before Director sees draft. Implemented as SREV verdict-based routing. Codified in `technology.md §7.3`.
- **"Fly the plane"** (Director directive 17:05) — PA is flight crew driving pipeline; Director is instructor drawing route. PA must push next concrete action, not wait. Codified in BEHAVIOR_CONTRACT rule 1b.
- **No silent handoff / no silent failure** (Director directive 16:48) — every task has objective + acceptance criteria + recipient ACK; on completion recipient reports back. Codified in `technology.md §7.2`.
- **English short industry role names** for all agents (Director directive 16:03) — Writer/Story Editor/Production Designer/Animator/Composer/Online Editor/Publicist/etc. Centralized in `lib/api/agent-names.ts` + PA AGENT_NAMES block.
- **Shot length 3-5s + gag floor 6-7s + Veo 8s hard cap** (Director directive 16:37) — codified in `technology.md §3.5`. Story Editor enforces via S09-S11 checks.
- **Sandy v02 = same slug + bump version** (Director directive 10:00) — rather than creating new character "Sandy 2", clone image from v01 LOCKED into v02 DRAFT, add full text canon, Director locks v02. Phase D Character Identity Model deferred.
- **q2 soft-archive over hard DELETE for S14 style cleanup** (Director directive 10:03) — REJECTED status with activity_event audit trail; preserves history; reversible. 13 APPROVED E01 final-cut shots preserved.
- **PA `q1n` reporting format** — short ≤5 word entries: "PLAN.md: brief description" + "CLAUDE.md: no change/brief description". Director-approved style.

